  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1111 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nSurface observations indicate that the reinforcing cold front is\nslowly sinking southeast. Dewpoints behind this boundary have\ndropped into the upper 40s and low 50s with values in the 60s in\nits wake. This front should clear the area by sunrise resulting\nin a cool, fall-like morning with temperatures in the 50s and\n60s.\n\nTemperatures will warm nicely in the dry air mass with plentiful\nsunshine on Monday, using max temperature values from the 75th\npercentile of the NBM. With the warming of temperatures and\nextremely dry air, expect minimum RH values to plummet each\nafternoon. Some areas, especially across north Mississippi, may\nfall below 25% or even 20%. This is a critical threshold for fire\nweather, so please monitor conditions if you plan on burning if\nyou are not under a burn ban. Expect this trend to continue\nthrough at least Wednesday as quasi-zonal flow dominates around\n500mb.\n\nOn Thursday, the flow aloft gets slightly disrupted as moisture\ntries to climb up the Delta, but will struggle due to the\nbattering ram of dry air aloft. Temperatures will heat up a bit,\nback into the upper 80s and lower 90s for the end of the work\nweek. The 12Z run of the ECMWF has backed off quite a bit on the\ninfluence of a tropical disturbance on the Mid-South late this\nweekend, while the GFS remains robust with this system. The LREF\nis also following suit with the ECMWF, so this will be something\nto monitor.\n\nDNM",
